Retails Sales Performance Analysis Dashboard
Objective

To analyze retail sales data using Microsoft Excel and Create an interactive dashboard that helps identify sales performance across products, regions, customer types, payment methods 
salespeople, and store Locations

Tools Used

.Microsoft Excel
.Excel Formulas
.PivotTables
.PivotCharts
.Excel Dashboard
.Data Cleaning
.Data Analysis

Key Metrics

- Total Orders: 1,500
- Total Quantity Sold: 10,467
- Total Net Sales: $4,338,731.489

Analysis Performed

- Analyzed net sales by region.
- Analyzed net sales by products.
- Compared Sales by customer type.
- Compared Sales by payment method.
- Evaluated Salesperson performance.
- Analyzed Sales by store location.
- Identified best-selling products based on quantity sold.
- Created KPI metrics and visual dashboard charts.

Business Insights

- Identified differences in sales performance across regions and store location.
- Compared Product performance using both net sales and quantity sold.
- Evaluated customer types to understand purchasing patterns.
- Compared payment methods to understand how customers complete purchases.
- Evaluated salesperson performance using net sales.
- Used dashboard KPIs to provide a quick overview of overall sales performance.

Business insights

- The West region generated the highest net sales, totalling $845,802.319
- Laptop generated the highest net sales among all products,totalling $677,979.8015
- Tablets were the best-selling products by quantity, with 2,577 unit sold
- Eva was the top-performing salesperson, generating $692,444.8095 in net sales
- Store Location D generated the highest net sales, totalling $1,194,454.13
- Retail customers generated the highest net sales, contributing $2,175,191.263
- Online payments generated the highest net sales among payment methods, totalling $962,127.87